Below is a structured Markdown table summarizing key concepts across Agile, Architecture, DDD, Best Practices, Design Patterns, Azure, AI, .NET, APIs, Databases, DI/Testing, Logging, Frontend, Version Control, and IDEs.

## Agile & Collaboration

| Topic                      | Description                                                  |
| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Scrum                      | Agile framework for iterative, incremental software delivery. |
| Kanban                     | Visual workflow method to manage and improve work in progress. |
| Jira                       | Agile project management and issue tracking tool.            |
| Miro                       | Online collaborative whiteboard for brainstorming and planning. |
| [Draw.io](https://Draw.io) | Diagramming tool for workflows, architectures, and processes. |

## Architectures

| Topic              | Description                                                  |
| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Microservices      | Architecture of small, independent, loosely coupled services. |
| Modular Monolith   | Monolithic app split into independent, well-defined modules. |
| Vertical Slice     | Feature-based architecture delivering full-stack functionality. |
| Hexagonal          | Ports-and-adapters architecture for decoupled, testable systems. |
| Clean Architecture | Layered design separating concerns for maintainability.      |
| Monolithic         | Single-tiered application where all components are unified.  |
| MVC                | Model-View-Controller pattern for separating UI, logic, and data. |

## Domain-Driven Design (DDD) & Related Concepts

| Topic                         | Description                                                  |
| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Domain-Driven Design (DDD)    | Models software based on complex business domains.           |
| Test-Driven Development (TDD) | Write tests before code to guide development.                |
| CQRS                          | Separates read and write operations for scalability and clarity. |
| Mediator Pattern              | Centralizes communication between components.                |
| Repository Pattern            | Abstracts data access logic from business logic.             |

## Best Practices

| Topic      | Description                                                  |
| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Clean Code | Meaningful names, small functions, consistent formatting, avoid magic numbers/strings, error handling, comments. |
| SOLID      | SRP, OCP, LSP, ISP, DIP principles.                          |
| DRY        | Don’t Repeat Yourself.                                       |
| KISS       | Keep It Simple, Stupid.                                      |
| YAGNI      | You Aren’t Gonna Need It.                                    |

## Design Patterns

| Pattern   | Description                                                 |
| --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |
| Factory   | Creates objects without exposing creation logic.            |
| Singleton | Ensures a class has only one instance globally.             |
| Builder   | Step-by-step object creation for complex structures.        |
| Decorator | Adds behavior to objects dynamically without altering code. |
| Observer  | Notifies subscribers automatically when state changes.      |
| Strategy  | Defines interchangeable algorithms for a task.              |

